Chapter: WGSL Emitter
  cites Foreword chapter CCE
  cites Foreword chapter StringUtils

 Generates WGSL (WebGPU Shading Language) compute shaders from the Codex
 typed IR. Unlike the PTX and SPIR-V plugs, WGSL is a high-level
 structured language: no SSA, no basic blocks, real if/else and operators,
 and storage buffers instead of raw pointers.

 A function whose last parameter is named "gid" (and which has at least two
 parameters) is treated as a compute kernel. Its buffer parameters -- the
 ones used as the base of a device-load/device-store -- become module-scope
 storage bindings; its remaining scalar parameters become a uniform struct;
 gid comes from @builtin(global_invocation_id). Every other function becomes
 a plain WGSL helper function.

Section: Refusal

 A generator that answers where it cannot lower ships a plausible wrong
 shader, and nothing downstream can tell that from a correct one
 (L-BAILVALUE). Every construct this emitter does not implement emits an
 identifier that does not exist and says what it was, so the module fails at
 createShaderModule with the construct's name in the message, and
 codex/plugs/wgsl/run.ps1 refuses the run before an output file is written.

 The rules these refusals and the lowerings below are measured against are
 docs/Reference/WgslSpec.md, distilled from the W3C Candidate Recommendation
 Draft of 31 August 2026. Re-read it before changing anything here.

  wgsl-refuse : Text -> Text
  wgsl-refuse (what) = "CODEX_REFUSED_" & what

Section: Name Sanitization

 WGSL 3.7 refuses an identifier that spells a keyword or a reserved word, that
 is a single underscore, or that STARTS with two underscores. Codex names hit
 all three: `type`, `match`, `mod`, `set`, `use` and `where` are ordinary Codex
 words and reserved in WGSL, and the compiler generates `__` names of its own.
 A name that trips any of these is prefixed rather than mangled, so what comes
 out still reads as the Codex name.

 The last clause is not a spec rule but a consequence of one. WGSL built-in
 function names are PREDECLARED, not reserved, so `fn min(...)` is legal and
 hides the built-in over the whole module (3.6, and the spec's own example).
 This emitter lowers real-min onto `min`, so a chapter with a helper named
 `min` would silently retarget every one of those calls and validate clean.
 Only the names this emitter actually emits are held back; anything else a
 program wants to call `mix` or `step` is its own business.

  wgsl-reserved-words : Text =
   " NULL Self abstract active alignas alignof as asm asm_fragment async attribute auto await become cast catch class co_await co_return co_yield coherent column_major common compile compile_fragment concept const_cast consteval constexpr constinit crate debugger decltype delete demote demote_to_helper do dynamic_cast enum explicit export extends extern external fallthrough filter final finally friend from fxgroup get goto groupshared highp impl implements import inline instanceof interface layout lowp macro macro_rules match mediump meta mod module move mut mutable namespace new nil noexcept noinline nointerpolation non_coherent noncoherent noperspective null nullptr of operator package packoffset partition pass patch pixelfragment precise precision premerge priv protected pub public readonly ref regardless register reinterpret_cast require resource restrict self set shared sizeof smooth snorm static static_assert static_cast std subroutine super target template this thread_local throw trait try type typedef typeid typename typeof union unless unorm unsafe unsized use using varying virtual volatile wgsl where with writeonly yield "

  wgsl-keywords : Text =
   " alias break case const const_assert continue continuing default diagnostic discard else enable false fn for if let loop override requires return struct switch true var while "

  wgsl-emitter-owned : Text =
   " sin cos tan sqrt abs min max floor ceil f32 i32 u32 bool select bitcast array ptr arrayLength "

  wgsl-taken : Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-taken (n) =
   let probe = " " & n & " "
   in if text-contains wgsl-keywords probe then True
   else if text-contains wgsl-reserved-words probe then True
   else text-contains wgsl-emitter-owned probe

  wgsl-sanitize : Text -> Text
  wgsl-sanitize (name) =
   let u = text-replace name "-" "_"
   in if u == "_" then "cdx_underscore"
   else if text-starts-with u "__" then "cdx" & u
   else if wgsl-taken u then "cdx_" & u
   else u

Section: Context

  WgslCtx = record {
   type-defs : List ATypeDef,
   indent : Text,
   buffers : List Text,
   kprefix : Text
  }

  empty-wgsl-ctx : List ATypeDef -> WgslCtx
  empty-wgsl-ctx (tds) =
   WgslCtx { type-defs = tds, indent = "  ", buffers = [], kprefix = "" }

  wgsl-contains : List Text, Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-contains (xs) (name) =
   wgsl-contains-loop xs name 0

  wgsl-contains-loop : List Text, Text, Integer -> Boolean
  wgsl-contains-loop (xs) (name) (i) =
   if i >= list-length xs then False
   else if (list-at xs i) == name then True
   else wgsl-contains-loop xs name (i + 1)

  wgsl-buf-name : WgslCtx, Text -> Text
  wgsl-buf-name (ctx) (base) =
   if ctx.kprefix == "" then "(*" & wgsl-sanitize base & ")"
   else ctx.kprefix & "_" & wgsl-sanitize base & "_buf"

Section: Float Support

 Codex Real is f64; WGSL has only f32. IrNumLit carries the f64 bit pattern,
 which we convert to f32 bits and emit as a bitcast literal (exact to f32).
 Storage buffers stay i32 -- only in-kernel math is float -- so device-load and
 device-store coerce at the boundary. Field extraction uses raw bit ops so it
 is correct regardless of the sign bit.

  wgsl-is-real : CodexType -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-real (ty) =
   when ty
    is RealTy (w) (m) -> True
    is FunTy (param) (fnrow) (ret) -> wgsl-is-real ret
    is EffectfulTy (names) (texts) (inner) -> wgsl-is-real inner
    is otherwise -> False

  wgsl-ty-text : CodexType -> Text
  wgsl-ty-text (ty) = if wgsl-is-real ty then "f32" else "i32"

  wgsl-f32-bits : Integer -> Integer
  wgsl-f32-bits (n) =
   let sign = bit-and (bit-shru n 63) 1
   in let exp = bit-and (bit-shru n 52) 2047
   in let mant = bit-and n 4503599627370495
   in let mant32 = bit-shru mant 29
   in if exp == 0 then bit-shl sign 31
   else if exp == 2047 then bit-or (bit-shl sign 31) (bit-or (bit-shl 255 23) mant32)
   else let exp32 = exp - 1023 + 127
   in if exp32 <= 0 then bit-shl sign 31
   else if exp32 >= 255 then bit-or (bit-shl sign 31) (bit-shl 255 23)
   else bit-or (bit-shl sign 31) (bit-or (bit-shl exp32 23) mant32)

  wgsl-f32-lit : Integer -> Text
  wgsl-f32-lit (n) = "bitcast<f32>(" & integer-to-text (wgsl-f32-bits n) & "u)"

 Codex Integer is 64-bit and WGSL i32 is not, and WGSL REFUSES a constant it
 cannot represent rather than wrapping it: the opaque-alpha idiom 255 * 16777216
 is 0xFF000000, and Chrome answers "value 4278190080 cannot be represented as
 i32". A value that still fits u32 is emitted as a bitcast, which is the same
 move wgsl-f32-lit already makes and gives the bit pattern the program meant.
 Above u32 there is nothing honest to emit, so it is left to fail loudly.

  wgsl-i32-max : Integer = 2147483647

  wgsl-u32-max : Integer = 4294967295

  wgsl-i32-lit : Integer -> Text
  wgsl-i32-lit (n) =
   if n > wgsl-i32-max then
    if n <= wgsl-u32-max then "bitcast<i32>(" & integer-to-text n & "u)"
    else wgsl-refuse "integer_literal_wider_than_32_bits"
   else if n < wgsl-i32-min then wgsl-refuse "integer_literal_below_i32_min"
   else integer-to-text n

  wgsl-fexpr : WgslCtx, IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-fexpr (ctx) (e) =
   if wgsl-is-real (ir-expr-type e) then wgsl-expr ctx e
   else "f32(" & wgsl-expr ctx e & ")"

  wgsl-iexpr : WgslCtx, IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-iexpr (ctx) (e) =
   if wgsl-is-real (ir-expr-type e) then "i32(" & wgsl-expr ctx e & ")"
   else wgsl-expr ctx e

Section: Binary Op Mapping

  wgsl-bin-op : IRBinaryOp -> Text
  wgsl-bin-op (op) =
   when op
    is IrAddInt -> "+"
    is IrSubInt -> "-"
    is IrMulInt -> "*"
    is IrDivInt -> "/"
    is IrRemInt -> "%"
    is IrPowInt -> "CODEX_REFUSED_integer_exponentiation"
    is IrAddNum | IrAddVec | IrAddRealApprox | IrAddRealTrapping | IrAddRealSaturating -> "+"
    is IrSubNum | IrSubVec | IrSubRealApprox | IrSubRealTrapping | IrSubRealSaturating -> "-"
    is IrMulNum | IrMulVec | IrMulRealApprox | IrMulRealTrapping | IrMulRealSaturating -> "*"
    is IrDivNum | IrDivVec | IrDivRealApprox | IrDivRealTrapping | IrDivRealSaturating -> "/"
    is IrEq -> "=="
    is IrNotEq -> "!="
    is IrLt | IrLtVec -> "<"
    is IrGt | IrGtVec -> ">"
    is IrLtEq | IrLtEqVec -> "<="
    is IrGtEq | IrGtEqVec -> ">="
    is IrAnd -> "&&"
    is IrOr -> "||"
    is IrAppendText -> "CODEX_REFUSED_text_append"
    is IrAppendList -> "CODEX_REFUSED_list_append"
    is IrConsList -> "CODEX_REFUSED_list_cons"
    is IrApproxEq -> "CODEX_REFUSED_approximate_equality"
    is IrApproxEqExact -> "CODEX_REFUSED_approximate_equality_exact"

 WGSL 8.7 spells the SHORT-CIRCUITING boolean operators && and ||, and gives
 & and | a second, non-short-circuiting meaning on bool. Both validate, so
 lowering Codex's `and` to & produced a module that compiled and evaluated the
 right operand unconditionally. The five below have no WGSL spelling at all:
 there is no exponentiation operator (pow is float-only), no text and no list,
 and an approximate equality lowered to == is a different question being
 answered. Each emits a token that is a parse error where it lands rather than
 a plausible operator, so nothing can carry it into a shipped shader.

  wgsl-op-refused : IRBinaryOp -> Boolean
  wgsl-op-refused (op) =
   when op
    is IrPowInt | IrAppendText | IrAppendList | IrConsList -> True
    is IrApproxEq | IrApproxEqExact -> True
    is otherwise -> False

  wgsl-op-logical : IRBinaryOp -> Boolean
  wgsl-op-logical (op) =
   when op
    is IrAnd | IrOr -> True
    is otherwise -> False

Section: Math Intrinsics

  wgsl-is-math-intrinsic : Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-math-intrinsic (name) =
   if name == "cordic-sin" then True
   else if name == "cordic-cos" then True
   else if name == "cordic-tan" then True
   else if name == "real-sin" then True
   else if name == "real-cos" then True
   else if name == "real-sqrt" then True
   else if name == "real-abs" then True
   else if name == "real-min" then True
   else if name == "real-max" then True
   else if name == "real-floor" then True
   else if name == "real-ceil" then True
   else if name == "real-from-int" then True
   else if name == "real-to-int" then True
   else if name == "__int-to-real" then True
   else if name == "__real-to-int" then True
   else False

  wgsl-math-builtin : Text -> Text
  wgsl-math-builtin (name) =
   if name == "cordic-sin" then "sin"
   else if name == "cordic-cos" then "cos"
   else if name == "cordic-tan" then "tan"
   else if name == "real-sin" then "sin"
   else if name == "real-cos" then "cos"
   else if name == "real-sqrt" then "sqrt"
   else if name == "real-abs" then "abs"
   else if name == "real-min" then "min"
   else if name == "real-max" then "max"
   else if name == "real-floor" then "floor"
   else if name == "real-ceil" then "ceil"
   else if name == "real-from-int" then "f32"
   else if name == "real-to-int" then "i32"
   else if name == "__int-to-real" then "f32"
   else if name == "__real-to-int" then "i32"
   else name

Section: Bit Intrinsics

 Codex spells the bit operations as builtin CALLS, so before this they reached
 the generic apply path and came out as bit_and(a, b): a function WGSL does not
 have. The whole set is in the language (8.10), and two of its rules differ
 from every other binary operator, which is why this is not a line in the
 operator table:

 The right operand of << and >> must be u32. An i32 shift count does not
 compile, and it is the operand type every other operator would have wanted.

 >> on a signed left operand is ARITHMETIC: "If e1 is negative, each inserted
 bit is 1". Codex bit-shr is that shift, and bit-shru is the logical one, so
 bit-shru has to go out through u32 and come back.

 The shift amount is the count modulo the bit width at run time, and a count at
 or past the width is an error only when it is a const-expression. Masking with
 31u is that same modulo written down: it changes no legal program's meaning
 and removes the const-expression error case.

  wgsl-is-bit-intrinsic : Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-bit-intrinsic (name) =
   if name == "bit-and" then True
   else if name == "bit-or" then True
   else if name == "bit-xor" then True
   else if name == "bit-not" then True
   else if name == "bit-shl" then True
   else if name == "bit-shr" then True
   else if name == "bit-shru" then True
   else False

  wgsl-iexpr-at : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-iexpr-at (ctx) (e) (depth) =
   if wgsl-is-real (ir-expr-type e) then "i32(" & wgsl-expr-at ctx e (depth + 1) & ")"
   else wgsl-expr-at ctx e (depth + 1)

  wgsl-shift-count : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-shift-count (ctx) (e) (depth) =
   "(u32(" & wgsl-iexpr-at ctx e depth & ") & 31u)"

  wgsl-emit-bit : WgslCtx, Text, List IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-bit (ctx) (name) (args) (depth) =
   if name == "bit-not" then
    (if list-length args < 1 then wgsl-refuse "bit_not_arity"
     else "(~" & wgsl-iexpr-at ctx (list-at args 0) depth & ")")
   else if list-length args < 2 then wgsl-refuse "bit_op_arity"
   else let a = wgsl-iexpr-at ctx (list-at args 0) depth
   in let b = wgsl-iexpr-at ctx (list-at args 1) depth
   in let sh = wgsl-shift-count ctx (list-at args 1) depth
   in if name == "bit-and" then "(" & a & " & " & b & ")"
   else if name == "bit-or" then "(" & a & " | " & b & ")"
   else if name == "bit-xor" then "(" & a & " ^ " & b & ")"
   else if name == "bit-shl" then "(" & a & " << " & sh & ")"
   else if name == "bit-shr" then "(" & a & " >> " & sh & ")"
   else "bitcast<i32>(bitcast<u32>(" & a & ") >> " & sh & ")"

 Storage buffers are emitted as array<i32> (wgsl-emit-buffer-decls), so the
 f64 forms are recognised here, which is what makes buffer discovery find their
 base, and then refused at emission: reading array<i32> for a value the source
 said was a Real hands back the wrong number with nothing to see. A float
 buffer needs an array<f32> binding and a second element type through the whole
 discovery path, which is a capability rather than a patch.

  wgsl-is-f64-device-op : Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-f64-device-op (name) =
   if name == "device-load-f64" then True
   else if name == "device-store-f64" then True
   else False

  wgsl-is-device-load : Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-device-load (name) =
   if name == "device-load" then True
   else if name == "device-load-f64" then True
   else False

  wgsl-is-device-store : Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-device-store (name) =
   if name == "device-store" then True
   else if name == "device-store-f64" then True
   else False

Section: Expression Emission

  wgsl-expr : WgslCtx, IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-expr (ctx) (e) = wgsl-expr-at ctx e 0

  wgsl-expr-at : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-expr-at (ctx) (e) (depth) =
   if depth >= 256 then wgsl-refuse "expression_nested_past_256"
   else when e
    is IrIntLit (n) (sp) -> wgsl-i32-lit n
    is IrNumLit (n) (sp) -> wgsl-f32-lit n
    is IrBoolLit (b) (sp) -> if b then "true" else "false"
    is IrCharLit (n) (sp) -> integer-to-text n
    is IrTextLit (s) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "text_literal"
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     if n == "True" then "true"
     else if n == "False" then "false"
     else wgsl-sanitize n
    is IrBinary (op) (l) (r) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-emit-binary ctx op l r ty
    is IrNegate (operand) (nty) (sp) ->
     "(-" & wgsl-expr-at ctx operand (depth + 1) & ")"
    is IrIf (cond) (th) (el) (ty) (sp) ->
     "select(" & wgsl-expr-at ctx el (depth + 1) & ", " & wgsl-expr-at ctx th (depth + 1) & ", " & wgsl-expr-at ctx cond (depth + 1) & ")"
    is IrLet (name) (ty) (val) (body) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-at ctx (wgsl-subst-expr body name val (depth + 1)) (depth + 1)
    is IrApply (f) (a) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-apply ctx e depth
    is IrLambda (params) (body) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-at ctx body (depth + 1)
    is IrList (elems) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "list_literal"
    is IrMatch (scrut) (branches) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "when_expression"
    is IrAct (stmts) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "act_block_in_expression_position"
    is IrHandle (eff) (body) (clauses) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-at ctx body (depth + 1)
    is IrWithTimeout (secs) (effs) (scopes) (body) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-at ctx body (depth + 1)
    is IrRecord (name) (fields) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "record_construction"
    is IrFieldAccess (rec) (field) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-at ctx rec (depth + 1) & "." & wgsl-sanitize field
    is IrFieldStore (rec) (field) (val) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "field_store"
    is IrFork (body) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-at ctx body (depth + 1)
    is IrAwait (task) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-expr-at ctx task (depth + 1)
    is IrTry (max) (body) (fb) (fail-stmts) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "try_expression"
    is IrError (msg) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-refuse "error_expression"

  wgsl-subst-expr : IRExpr, Text, IRExpr, Integer -> IRExpr
  wgsl-subst-expr (e) (n) (rep) (depth) =
   if depth >= 256 then e
   else when e
    is IrName (m) (ty) (sp) -> if m == n then rep else e
    is IrBinary (op) (l) (r) (ty) (sp) -> IrBinary op (wgsl-subst-expr l n rep (depth + 1)) (wgsl-subst-expr r n rep (depth + 1)) ty sp
    is IrNegate (o) (nty) (sp) -> IrNegate (wgsl-subst-expr o n rep (depth + 1)) nty sp
    is IrIf (c) (tb) (el) (ty) (sp) -> IrIf (wgsl-subst-expr c n rep (depth + 1)) (wgsl-subst-expr tb n rep (depth + 1)) (wgsl-subst-expr el n rep (depth + 1)) ty sp
    is IrLet (nm) (ty) (v) (b) (sp) -> IrLet nm ty (wgsl-subst-expr v n rep (depth + 1)) (if nm == n then b else wgsl-subst-expr b n rep (depth + 1)) sp
    is IrApply (f) (a) (ty) (sp) -> IrApply (wgsl-subst-expr f n rep (depth + 1)) (wgsl-subst-expr a n rep (depth + 1)) ty sp
    is IrFieldAccess (r) (fld) (ty) (sp) -> IrFieldAccess (wgsl-subst-expr r n rep (depth + 1)) fld ty sp
    is otherwise -> e

  wgsl-expr-apply : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-expr-apply (ctx) (e) (depth) =
   let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
   in when (chain.root)
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     if n == "__narrow" then wgsl-expr-at ctx (list-at (chain.args) 0) (depth + 1)
     else if wgsl-is-f64-device-op n then wgsl-refuse "float_storage_buffer_access"
     else if wgsl-is-device-load n then wgsl-emit-device-load ctx (chain.args) depth
     else if wgsl-is-bit-intrinsic n then wgsl-emit-bit ctx n (chain.args) depth
     else if wgsl-is-math-intrinsic n then wgsl-math-builtin n & "(" & wgsl-emit-fargs ctx (chain.args) depth & ")"
     else wgsl-sanitize n & "(" & wgsl-emit-args ctx (chain.args) depth & ")"
    is otherwise -> wgsl-refuse "call_through_a_computed_callee"

  wgsl-emit-device-load : WgslCtx, List IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-device-load (ctx) (args) (depth) =
   if list-length args < 2 then wgsl-refuse "device_load_arity"
   else let base = list-at args 0
   in let idx = list-at args 1
   in wgsl-load-base ctx base & "[" & wgsl-expr-at ctx idx (depth + 1) & "]"

  wgsl-load-base : WgslCtx, IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-load-base (ctx) (base) =
   when base
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-buf-name ctx n
    is otherwise -> wgsl-refuse "buffer_base_that_is_not_a_name"

  wgsl-emit-args : WgslCtx, List IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-args (ctx) (args) (depth) =
   wgsl-emit-args-loop ctx args 0 "" depth

  wgsl-emit-args-loop : WgslCtx, List IRExpr, Integer, Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-args-loop (ctx) (args) (i) (acc) (depth) =
   if i >= list-length args then acc
   else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else ", "
   in let piece = wgsl-arg-piece ctx (list-at args i) depth
   in wgsl-emit-args-loop ctx args (i + 1) (acc & sep & piece) depth

  wgsl-arg-piece : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-arg-piece (ctx) (a) (depth) =
   when a
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     if wgsl-contains (ctx.buffers) n then
      (if ctx.kprefix == "" then wgsl-sanitize n
       else "&" & ctx.kprefix & "_" & wgsl-sanitize n & "_buf")
     else wgsl-expr-at ctx a (depth + 1)
    is otherwise -> wgsl-expr-at ctx a (depth + 1)

  wgsl-i32-min : Integer = 0 - 2147483648

  wgsl-is-int-lit : IRExpr -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-int-lit (e) =
   when e
    is IrIntLit (n) (sp) -> True
    is otherwise -> False

  wgsl-int-lit-val : IRExpr -> Integer
  wgsl-int-lit-val (e) =
   when e
    is IrIntLit (n) (sp) -> n
    is otherwise -> 0

  wgsl-folds : IRBinaryOp -> Boolean
  wgsl-folds (op) =
   when op
    is IrAddInt | IrSubInt | IrMulInt -> True
    is otherwise -> False

  wgsl-fold-int : IRBinaryOp, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  wgsl-fold-int (op) (a) (b) =
   when op
    is IrAddInt -> a + b
    is IrSubInt -> a - b
    is IrMulInt -> a * b
    is otherwise -> 0

 WGSL evaluates a constant expression at compile time and REFUSES one whose
 value its type cannot hold, so 255 * 16777216 is rejected even though both
 operands are in range. The plug IR is compiled with -Passes text-plug, which
 replaces the default pipeline and therefore runs no constant folding, so the
 multiply arrives here intact. Folding is done ONLY when the result is out of
 i32 range, which leaves every expression that already worked byte-identical.

  wgsl-const-fold-text : IRBinaryOp, IRExpr, IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-const-fold-text (op) (l) (r) =
   if wgsl-folds op then
    if wgsl-is-int-lit l then
     if wgsl-is-int-lit r then
      let v = wgsl-fold-int op (wgsl-int-lit-val l) (wgsl-int-lit-val r)
      in if v > wgsl-i32-max then wgsl-i32-lit v
         else if v < wgsl-i32-min then wgsl-i32-lit v
         else ""
     else ""
    else ""
   else ""

  wgsl-emit-binary : WgslCtx, IRBinaryOp, IRExpr, IRExpr, CodexType -> Text
  wgsl-emit-binary (ctx) (op) (l) (r) (ty) =
   if (wgsl-is-real ty | wgsl-is-real (ir-expr-type l)) | wgsl-is-real (ir-expr-type r) then
    "(" & wgsl-fexpr ctx l & " " & wgsl-bin-op op & " " & wgsl-fexpr ctx r & ")"
   else let folded = wgsl-const-fold-text op l r
   in if folded /= "" then folded
   else "(" & wgsl-iexpr ctx l & " " & wgsl-bin-op op & " " & wgsl-iexpr ctx r & ")"

  wgsl-emit-fargs : WgslCtx, List IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-fargs (ctx) (args) (depth) =
   wgsl-emit-fargs-loop ctx args 0 ""

  wgsl-emit-fargs-loop : WgslCtx, List IRExpr, Integer, Text -> Text
  wgsl-emit-fargs-loop (ctx) (args) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length args then acc
   else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else ", "
   in wgsl-emit-fargs-loop ctx args (i + 1) (acc & sep & wgsl-fexpr ctx (list-at args i))

Section: Statement Body Emission

  wgsl-body : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Boolean, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-body (ctx) (e) (is-kernel) (depth) =
   if depth >= 256 then ctx.indent & "return " & wgsl-refuse "body_nested_past_256" & ";\n"
   else when e
    is IrLet (name) (ty) (val) (body) (sp) ->
     ctx.indent & "let " & wgsl-sanitize name & " = " & wgsl-expr ctx val & ";\n"
      & wgsl-body ctx body is-kernel (depth + 1)
    is IrIf (cond) (th) (el) (ty) (sp) ->
     ctx.indent & "if (" & wgsl-expr ctx cond & ") {\n"
      & wgsl-body ctx th is-kernel (depth + 1)
      & ctx.indent & "} else {\n"
      & wgsl-body ctx el is-kernel (depth + 1)
      & ctx.indent & "}\n"
    is IrAct (stmts) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-act ctx stmts is-kernel 0 depth
    is IrApply (f) (a) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-body-tail ctx e is-kernel depth
    is otherwise ->
     wgsl-body-tail ctx e is-kernel depth

  wgsl-body-tail : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Boolean, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-body-tail (ctx) (e) (is-kernel) (depth) =
   let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
   in when (chain.root)
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     if wgsl-is-f64-device-op n then
      ctx.indent & "_ = " & wgsl-refuse "float_storage_buffer_access" & ";\n"
     else if wgsl-is-device-store n then
      wgsl-emit-device-store ctx (chain.args) depth
       & (if is-kernel then "" else ctx.indent & "return 0;\n")
     else wgsl-tail-value ctx e is-kernel
    is otherwise -> wgsl-tail-value ctx e is-kernel

  wgsl-tail-value : WgslCtx, IRExpr, Boolean -> Text
  wgsl-tail-value (ctx) (e) (is-kernel) =
   if is-kernel then ctx.indent & "_ = " & wgsl-expr ctx e & ";\n"
   else ctx.indent & "return " & wgsl-expr ctx e & ";\n"

  wgsl-emit-device-store : WgslCtx, List IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-device-store (ctx) (args) (depth) =
   if list-length args < 3 then ctx.indent & "_ = " & wgsl-refuse "device_store_arity" & ";\n"
   else let base = list-at args 0
   in let idx = list-at args 1
   in let val = list-at args 2
   in ctx.indent & wgsl-load-base ctx base & "[" & wgsl-expr ctx idx & "] = " & wgsl-iexpr ctx val & ";\n"

  wgsl-is-store-expr : IRExpr -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-store-expr (e) =
   let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
   in when (chain.root)
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-is-device-store n
    is otherwise -> False

  wgsl-store-stmt : WgslCtx, IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-store-stmt (ctx) (e) =
   let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
   in if wgsl-store-is-f64 (chain.root) then
    ctx.indent & "_ = " & wgsl-refuse "float_storage_buffer_access" & ";\n"
   else wgsl-emit-device-store ctx (chain.args) 0

  wgsl-store-is-f64 : IRExpr -> Boolean
  wgsl-store-is-f64 (root) =
   when root
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-is-f64-device-op n
    is otherwise -> False

Section: Act Block Emission

  wgsl-act : WgslCtx, List IRActStmt, Boolean, Integer, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-act (ctx) (stmts) (is-kernel) (i) (depth) =
   if i >= list-length stmts then (if is-kernel then "" else ctx.indent & "return 0;\n")
   else let s = list-at stmts i
   in let is-last = i == list-length stmts - 1
   in when s
    is IrDoBind (name) (ty) (val) (sp) ->
     (if wgsl-is-store-expr val then wgsl-store-stmt ctx val
      else ctx.indent & "let " & wgsl-sanitize name & " = " & wgsl-expr ctx val & ";\n")
      & wgsl-act ctx stmts is-kernel (i + 1) depth
    is IrDoExec (e) (sp) ->
     if is-last then wgsl-body ctx e is-kernel (depth + 1)
     else (if wgsl-is-store-expr e then wgsl-store-stmt ctx e
           else ctx.indent & "_ = " & wgsl-expr ctx e & ";\n")
      & wgsl-act ctx stmts is-kernel (i + 1) depth

Section: Buffer Discovery

  wgsl-collect-buffers : IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-collect-buffers (e) (acc) =
   when e
    is IrApply (f) (a) (ty) (sp) ->
     let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
     in let acc1 = wgsl-scan-apply-base (chain.root) (chain.args) acc
     in wgsl-collect-args (chain.args) acc1
    is IrLet (name) (ty) (val) (body) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-buffers body (wgsl-collect-buffers val acc)
    is IrIf (cond) (th) (el) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-buffers el (wgsl-collect-buffers th (wgsl-collect-buffers cond acc))
    is IrBinary (op) (l) (r) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-buffers r (wgsl-collect-buffers l acc)
    is IrNegate (operand) (nty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-buffers operand acc
    is IrAct (stmts) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-act stmts acc 0
    is otherwise -> acc

  wgsl-scan-apply-base : IRExpr, List IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-scan-apply-base (root) (args) (acc) =
   when root
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     if (wgsl-is-device-load n | wgsl-is-device-store n) then
      (if list-length args >= 1 then wgsl-add-base (list-at args 0) acc else acc)
     else acc
    is otherwise -> acc

  wgsl-add-base : IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-add-base (base) (acc) =
   when base
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) -> if wgsl-contains acc n then acc else list-push acc n
    is otherwise -> acc

  wgsl-collect-args : List IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-collect-args (args) (acc) =
   wgsl-collect-args-loop args acc 0

  wgsl-collect-args-loop : List IRExpr, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-collect-args-loop (args) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length args then acc
   else wgsl-collect-args-loop args (wgsl-collect-buffers (list-at args i) acc) (i + 1)

  wgsl-collect-act : List IRActStmt, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-collect-act (stmts) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length stmts then acc
   else let s = list-at stmts i
   in when s
    is IrDoBind (name) (ty) (val) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-act stmts (wgsl-collect-buffers val acc) (i + 1)
    is IrDoExec (e) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-act stmts (wgsl-collect-buffers e acc) (i + 1)

Section: Buffer Forwarding

 wgsl-collect-buffers reads ONE body, so a parameter that is a buffer only by
 being PASSED ON is invisible to it. `earth-pixel` forwards `framebuf` and
 `tex` to `earth-shade-pixel`, and `bh-pixel` forwards `framebuf` two hops
 through the self-recursive `bh-march`. Such a parameter was typed i32 and, in
 a kernel, became a uniform scalar rather than a storage binding, so the call
 failed against the callee's pointer parameter with `got 'i32'`.

 Everything downstream already handles a buffer parameter: wgsl-arg-piece
 emits the binding address at the call site, wgsl-emit-params-b types the
 pointer, and the loop lowering holds it out of the parameter moves. Only the
 SET was wrong, so the forwarding is resolved to a fixpoint here, before
 anything is emitted. Two rounds settle the globe kernels; the cap is a
 termination guard, not a limit anyone should reach.

  BufEntry = record {
   be-name : Text,
   be-bufs : List Text
  }

  wgsl-bufs-of : List BufEntry, Text -> List Text
  wgsl-bufs-of (m) (n) = wgsl-bufs-of-loop m n 0

  wgsl-bufs-of-loop : List BufEntry, Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-bufs-of-loop (m) (n) (i) =
   if i >= list-length m then []
   else let e = list-at m i
   in if e.be-name == n then e.be-bufs
   else wgsl-bufs-of-loop m n (i + 1)

  wgsl-param-has : List IRParam, Text -> Boolean
  wgsl-param-has (ps) (n) = wgsl-param-has-loop ps n 0

  wgsl-param-has-loop : List IRParam, Text, Integer -> Boolean
  wgsl-param-has-loop (ps) (n) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then False
   else if (list-at ps i).name == n then True
   else wgsl-param-has-loop ps n (i + 1)

  wgsl-callee-param-name : List IRDef, Text, Integer, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-callee-param-name (defs) (cname) (idx) (i) =
   if i >= list-length defs then ""
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in if d.name == cname then
    (if idx < list-length (d.params) then (list-at (d.params) idx).name else "")
   else wgsl-callee-param-name defs cname idx (i + 1)

  wgsl-add-fwd : List IRParam, IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-add-fwd (ps) (a) (acc) =
   when a
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     if wgsl-param-has ps n then
      (if wgsl-contains acc n then acc else list-push acc n)
     else acc
    is otherwise -> acc

  wgsl-fwd-args : List IRDef, List BufEntry, List IRParam, Text, List IRExpr, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-fwd-args (defs) (m) (ps) (cname) (args) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length args then acc
   else let pn = wgsl-callee-param-name defs cname i 0
   in let hit = if pn == "" then False else wgsl-contains (wgsl-bufs-of m cname) pn
   in let acc1 = if hit then wgsl-add-fwd ps (list-at args i) acc else acc
   in wgsl-fwd-args defs m ps cname args acc1 (i + 1)

  wgsl-fwd-root : List IRDef, List BufEntry, List IRParam, IRExpr, List IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-fwd-root (defs) (m) (ps) (root) (args) (acc) =
   when root
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) -> wgsl-fwd-args defs m ps n args acc 0
    is otherwise -> acc

  wgsl-fwd-scan : List IRDef, List BufEntry, List IRParam, IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-fwd-scan (defs) (m) (ps) (e) (acc) =
   when e
    is IrApply (f) (a) (ty) (sp) ->
     let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
     in let acc1 = wgsl-fwd-root defs m ps (chain.root) (chain.args) acc
     in wgsl-fwd-scan-args defs m ps (chain.args) acc1 0
    is IrLet (n) (ty) (v) (b) (sp) ->
     wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps b (wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps v acc)
    is IrIf (c) (t) (el) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps el (wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps t (wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps c acc))
    is IrBinary (op) (l) (r) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps r (wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps l acc)
    is IrNegate (o) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps o acc
    is IrAct (stmts) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-fwd-scan-act defs m ps stmts acc 0
    is otherwise -> acc

  wgsl-fwd-scan-args : List IRDef, List BufEntry, List IRParam, List IRExpr, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-fwd-scan-args (defs) (m) (ps) (args) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length args then acc
   else wgsl-fwd-scan-args defs m ps args (wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps (list-at args i) acc) (i + 1)

  wgsl-fwd-scan-act : List IRDef, List BufEntry, List IRParam, List IRActStmt, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-fwd-scan-act (defs) (m) (ps) (stmts) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length stmts then acc
   else let s = list-at stmts i
   in when s
    is IrDoBind (n) (ty) (v) (sp) ->
     wgsl-fwd-scan-act defs m ps stmts (wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps v acc) (i + 1)
    is IrDoExec (e) (sp) ->
     wgsl-fwd-scan-act defs m ps stmts (wgsl-fwd-scan defs m ps e acc) (i + 1)

  wgsl-bufmap-init : List IRDef, Integer, List BufEntry -> List BufEntry
  wgsl-bufmap-init (defs) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length defs then acc
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in let e = BufEntry { be-name = d.name, be-bufs = wgsl-collect-buffers (d.body) [] }
   in wgsl-bufmap-init defs (i + 1) (list-push acc e)

  wgsl-bufmap-round : List IRDef, List BufEntry, Integer, List BufEntry -> List BufEntry
  wgsl-bufmap-round (defs) (m) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length defs then acc
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in let nb = wgsl-fwd-scan defs m (d.params) (d.body) (wgsl-bufs-of m (d.name))
   in wgsl-bufmap-round defs m (i + 1) (list-push acc (BufEntry { be-name = d.name, be-bufs = nb }))

  wgsl-bufmap-size : List BufEntry, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  wgsl-bufmap-size (m) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length m then acc
   else wgsl-bufmap-size m (i + 1) (acc + list-length ((list-at m i).be-bufs))

  wgsl-bufmap-fix : List IRDef, List BufEntry, Integer -> List BufEntry
  wgsl-bufmap-fix (defs) (m) (iters) =
   if iters <= 0 then m
   else let m2 = wgsl-bufmap-round defs m 0 []
   in if wgsl-bufmap-size m2 0 0 == wgsl-bufmap-size m 0 0 then m2
   else wgsl-bufmap-fix defs m2 (iters - 1)

  wgsl-bufmap : List IRDef -> List BufEntry
  wgsl-bufmap (defs) = wgsl-bufmap-fix defs (wgsl-bufmap-init defs 0 []) 8

Section: Function Classification

  wgsl-is-kernel : IRDef -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-kernel (d) =
   if list-length (d.params) < 2 then False
   else (list-at (d.params) (list-length (d.params) - 1)).name == "gid"

Section: Helper Function Emission

  wgsl-emit-params : List IRParam, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-params (params) (i) =
   if i >= list-length params then ""
   else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else ", "
   in let p = list-at params i
   in sep & wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & " : " & wgsl-ty-text (p.type-val) & wgsl-emit-params params (i + 1)

 A helper that uses a parameter as a device-load/store base takes that buffer as
 a storage pointer. hbufs is the set of such parameter names; the helper ctx
 carries them (kprefix empty) so device-load emits `(*p)[i]` and the parameter
 is typed `ptr<storage, array<i32>, read_write>`.

  wgsl-helper-ctx : WgslCtx, List Text -> WgslCtx
  wgsl-helper-ctx (ctx) (hbufs) =
   WgslCtx { type-defs = ctx.type-defs, indent = ctx.indent, buffers = hbufs, kprefix = "" }

  wgsl-emit-params-b : List IRParam, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-params-b (params) (bufs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length params then ""
   else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else ", "
   in let p = list-at params i
   in let ty = if wgsl-contains bufs (p.name) then "ptr<storage, array<i32>, read_write>" else wgsl-ty-text (p.type-val)
   in sep & wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & " : " & ty & wgsl-emit-params-b params bufs (i + 1)

  wgsl-emit-helper : WgslCtx, List BufEntry, IRDef -> Text
  wgsl-emit-helper (ctx) (bmap) (d) =
   let hbufs = wgsl-bufs-of bmap (d.name)
   in let hctx = wgsl-helper-ctx ctx hbufs
   in if wgsl-is-self-recursive d then wgsl-emit-loop-helper hctx d
   else let name = wgsl-sanitize (d.name)
   in let params = wgsl-emit-params-b (d.params) hbufs 0
   in let body = wgsl-body hctx (d.body) False 0
   in "fn " & name & "(" & params & ") -> " & wgsl-ty-text (d.type-val) & " {\n" & body & "}\n\n"

Section: Recursion to Loop

 WGSL has no recursion. A tail-self-recursive helper is lowered to a `loop`:
 its parameters become mutable `var`s, the base cases `return`, and each tail
 self-call becomes a parallel move of the arguments into the vars followed by
 `continue`. Arguments are evaluated into temporaries first so the moves do not
 clobber values still needed by later arguments.

  wgsl-is-self-recursive : IRDef -> Boolean
  wgsl-is-self-recursive (d) =
   wgsl-contains (wgsl-collect-calls (d.body) []) (d.name)

  wgsl-loop-params : List IRParam, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-params (ps) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then ""
   else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else ", "
   in let p = list-at ps i
   in sep & wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & "__a : " & wgsl-ty-text (p.type-val) & wgsl-loop-params ps (i + 1)

  wgsl-loop-vars : List IRParam, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-vars (ps) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then ""
   else let n = wgsl-sanitize ((list-at ps i).name)
   in "  var " & n & " = " & n & "__a;\n" & wgsl-loop-vars ps (i + 1)

  wgsl-loop-move-temps : WgslCtx, List IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-move-temps (ctx) (args) (i) =
   if i >= list-length args then ""
   else "    let _mv" & integer-to-text i & " = " & wgsl-expr ctx (list-at args i) & ";\n"
    & wgsl-loop-move-temps ctx args (i + 1)

  wgsl-loop-move-assign : List IRParam, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-move-assign (ps) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then ""
   else "    " & wgsl-sanitize ((list-at ps i).name) & " = _mv" & integer-to-text i & ";\n"
    & wgsl-loop-move-assign ps (i + 1)

  wgsl-loop-move : WgslCtx, List IRParam, List IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-loop-move (ctx) (ps) (args) =
   wgsl-loop-move-temps-b ctx ps args (ctx.buffers) 0 & wgsl-loop-move-assign-b ps (ctx.buffers) 0 & "    continue;\n"

  wgsl-loop-move-temps-b : WgslCtx, List IRParam, List IRExpr, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-move-temps-b (ctx) (ps) (args) (bufs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length args then ""
   else let is-buf = if i < list-length ps then wgsl-contains bufs ((list-at ps i).name) else False
   in let piece = if is-buf then "" else "    let _mv" & integer-to-text i & " = " & wgsl-expr ctx (list-at args i) & ";\n"
   in piece & wgsl-loop-move-temps-b ctx ps args bufs (i + 1)

  wgsl-loop-move-assign-b : List IRParam, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-move-assign-b (ps) (bufs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then ""
   else let p = list-at ps i
   in let piece = if wgsl-contains bufs (p.name) then "" else "    " & wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & " = _mv" & integer-to-text i & ";\n"
   in piece & wgsl-loop-move-assign-b ps bufs (i + 1)

  wgsl-loop-tail : WgslCtx, Text, List IRParam, IRExpr -> Text
  wgsl-loop-tail (ctx) (selfn) (ps) (e) =
   let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
   in when (chain.root)
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     if n == selfn then wgsl-loop-move ctx ps (chain.args)
     else "    return " & wgsl-expr ctx e & ";\n"
    is otherwise -> "    return " & wgsl-expr ctx e & ";\n"

  wgsl-loop-body : WgslCtx, Text, List IRParam, IRExpr, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-body (ctx) (selfn) (ps) (e) (depth) =
   if depth >= 256 then "    return " & wgsl-refuse "loop_body_nested_past_256" & ";\n"
   else when e
    is IrLet (n) (ty) (v) (b) (sp) ->
     "    let " & wgsl-sanitize n & " = " & wgsl-expr ctx v & ";\n"
      & wgsl-loop-body ctx selfn ps b (depth + 1)
    is IrIf (c) (t) (el) (ty) (sp) ->
     "    if (" & wgsl-expr ctx c & ") {\n"
      & wgsl-loop-body ctx selfn ps t (depth + 1)
      & "    } else {\n"
      & wgsl-loop-body ctx selfn ps el (depth + 1)
      & "    }\n"
    is IrAct (stmts) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-loop-act ctx selfn ps stmts 0 depth
    is otherwise ->
     wgsl-loop-tail ctx selfn ps e

  wgsl-loop-act : WgslCtx, Text, List IRParam, List IRActStmt, Integer, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-act (ctx) (selfn) (ps) (stmts) (i) (depth) =
   if i >= list-length stmts then "    return 0;\n"
   else let s = list-at stmts i
   in let is-last = i == list-length stmts - 1
   in when s
    is IrDoBind (name) (ty) (val) (sp) ->
     "    let " & wgsl-sanitize name & " = " & wgsl-expr ctx val & ";\n"
      & wgsl-loop-act ctx selfn ps stmts (i + 1) depth
    is IrDoExec (e) (sp) ->
     if is-last then wgsl-loop-body ctx selfn ps e (depth + 1)
     else "    _ = " & wgsl-expr ctx e & ";\n" & wgsl-loop-act ctx selfn ps stmts (i + 1) depth

  wgsl-loop-params-b : List IRParam, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-params-b (ps) (bufs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then ""
   else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else ", "
   in let p = list-at ps i
   in let piece = if wgsl-contains bufs (p.name)
      then wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & " : ptr<storage, array<i32>, read_write>"
      else wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & "__a : " & wgsl-ty-text (p.type-val)
   in sep & piece & wgsl-loop-params-b ps bufs (i + 1)

  wgsl-loop-vars-b : List IRParam, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-loop-vars-b (ps) (bufs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then ""
   else let p = list-at ps i
   in let piece = if wgsl-contains bufs (p.name) then ""
      else "  var " & wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & " = " & wgsl-sanitize (p.name) & "__a;\n"
   in piece & wgsl-loop-vars-b ps bufs (i + 1)

  wgsl-emit-loop-helper : WgslCtx, IRDef -> Text
  wgsl-emit-loop-helper (ctx) (d) =
   "fn " & wgsl-sanitize (d.name) & "(" & wgsl-loop-params-b (d.params) (ctx.buffers) 0 & ") -> " & wgsl-ty-text (d.type-val) & " {\n"
    & wgsl-loop-vars-b (d.params) (ctx.buffers) 0
    & "  loop {\n"
    & wgsl-loop-body ctx (d.name) (d.params) (d.body) 0
    & "  }\n}\n\n"

Section: Kernel Emission

  wgsl-scalar-params : List IRParam, List Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-scalar-params (params) (buffers) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length params then acc
   else let p = list-at params i
   in let is-gid = p.name == "gid"
   in let is-buf = wgsl-contains buffers (p.name)
   in let acc1 = if (is-gid | is-buf) then acc else list-push acc (p.name)
   in wgsl-scalar-params params buffers (i + 1) acc1

  wgsl-emit-buffer-decls : Text, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-buffer-decls (kprefix) (buffers) (i) =
   if i >= list-length buffers then ""
   else let b = list-at buffers i
   in "@group(0) @binding(" & integer-to-text i & ") var<storage, read_write> "
    & kprefix & "_" & wgsl-sanitize b & "_buf : array<i32>;\n"
    & wgsl-emit-buffer-decls kprefix buffers (i + 1)

 A uniform field was typed i32 whatever the parameter was, so a kernel with a
 Real scalar parameter declared an i32 field and then used it as an f32. WGSL
 has almost no implicit conversion (6.1.2), so that is a type error rather than
 a silent coercion, but it is the parameter's own type that decides it.

  wgsl-scalar-ty : List IRParam, Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-scalar-ty (ps) (n) (i) =
   if i >= list-length ps then "i32"
   else let p = list-at ps i
   in if p.name == n then wgsl-ty-text (p.type-val)
   else wgsl-scalar-ty ps n (i + 1)

  wgsl-emit-uniform-fields : List IRParam, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-uniform-fields (ps) (scalars) (i) =
   if i >= list-length scalars then ""
   else let n = list-at scalars i
   in "  " & wgsl-sanitize n & " : " & wgsl-scalar-ty ps n 0 & ",\n"
    & wgsl-emit-uniform-fields ps scalars (i + 1)

  wgsl-emit-scalar-lets : Text, Text, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-scalar-lets (indent) (uvar) (scalars) (i) =
   if i >= list-length scalars then ""
   else let s = wgsl-sanitize (list-at scalars i)
   in indent & "let " & s & " = " & uvar & "." & s & ";\n" & wgsl-emit-scalar-lets indent uvar scalars (i + 1)

  wgsl-emit-kernel : WgslCtx, List BufEntry, IRDef -> Text
  wgsl-emit-kernel (ctx) (bmap) (d) =
   let kname = wgsl-sanitize (d.name)
   in let buffers = wgsl-bufs-of bmap (d.name)
   in let scalars = wgsl-scalar-params (d.params) buffers 0 []
   in let kctx = WgslCtx { type-defs = ctx.type-defs, indent = "  ", buffers = buffers, kprefix = kname }
   in let buf-decls = wgsl-emit-buffer-decls kname buffers 0
   in let uvar = "u_" & kname
   in let has-scalars = list-length scalars > 0
   in let ubinding = integer-to-text (list-length buffers)
   in let uni-decl = if has-scalars then
       "struct U_" & kname & " {\n" & wgsl-emit-uniform-fields (d.params) scalars 0 & "}\n"
       & "@group(0) @binding(" & ubinding & ") var<uniform> " & uvar & " : U_" & kname & ";\n"
      else ""
   in let scalar-lets = if has-scalars then wgsl-emit-scalar-lets "  " uvar scalars 0 else ""
   in let body = wgsl-body kctx (d.body) True 0
   in buf-decls & uni-decl
    & "\n@compute @workgroup_size(64)\n"
    & "fn " & kname & "_main(@builtin(global_invocation_id) gid_vec : vec3<u32>) {\n"
    & "  let gid = i32(gid_vec.x);\n"
    & scalar-lets
    & body
    & "}\n\n"

Section: Reachability

  wgsl-add-name : Text, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-add-name (n) (acc) =
   if wgsl-contains acc n then acc else list-push acc n

  wgsl-collect-calls : IRExpr, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-collect-calls (e) (acc) =
   when e
    is IrApply (f) (a) (ty) (sp) ->
     let chain = collect-apply-chain e []
     in let acc1 = when (chain.root)
       is IrName (n) (nty) (nsp) -> wgsl-add-name n acc
       is otherwise -> acc
     in wgsl-collect-calls-args (chain.args) acc1 0
    is IrLet (name) (ty) (val) (body) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-calls body (wgsl-collect-calls val acc)
    is IrIf (cond) (th) (el) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-calls el (wgsl-collect-calls th (wgsl-collect-calls cond acc))
    is IrBinary (op) (l) (r) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-calls r (wgsl-collect-calls l acc)
    is IrNegate (operand) (nty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-calls operand acc
    is IrAct (stmts) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-calls-act stmts acc 0
    is IrName (n) (ty) (sp) ->
     wgsl-add-name n acc
    is otherwise -> acc

  wgsl-collect-calls-args : List IRExpr, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-collect-calls-args (args) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length args then acc
   else wgsl-collect-calls-args args (wgsl-collect-calls (list-at args i) acc) (i + 1)

  wgsl-collect-calls-act : List IRActStmt, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-collect-calls-act (stmts) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length stmts then acc
   else let s = list-at stmts i
   in when s
    is IrDoBind (name) (ty) (val) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-calls-act stmts (wgsl-collect-calls val acc) (i + 1)
    is IrDoExec (e) (sp) ->
     wgsl-collect-calls-act stmts (wgsl-collect-calls e acc) (i + 1)

  wgsl-kernel-calls : List IRDef, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-kernel-calls (defs) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length defs then acc
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in if wgsl-is-kernel d then wgsl-kernel-calls defs (wgsl-collect-calls (d.body) acc) (i + 1)
   else wgsl-kernel-calls defs acc (i + 1)

  wgsl-add-callees : List IRDef, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-add-callees (defs) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length defs then acc
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in if (((wgsl-is-kernel d) | (wgsl-contains acc (d.name) == False)) | wgsl-is-math-intrinsic (d.name)) then wgsl-add-callees defs acc (i + 1)
   else wgsl-add-callees defs (wgsl-collect-calls (d.body) acc) (i + 1)

  wgsl-expand-reach : List IRDef, List Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-expand-reach (defs) (acc) (iters) =
   if iters <= 0 then acc
   else wgsl-expand-reach defs (wgsl-add-callees defs acc 0) (iters - 1)

  wgsl-reachable : List IRDef -> List Text
  wgsl-reachable (defs) =
   let seed = wgsl-kernel-calls defs [] 0
   in wgsl-expand-reach defs seed (list-length defs)

  wgsl-has-kernel : List IRDef, Integer -> Boolean
  wgsl-has-kernel (defs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length defs then False
   else if wgsl-is-kernel (list-at defs i) then True
   else wgsl-has-kernel defs (i + 1)

Section: Chapter Emission

 The loop's progress test compares a length captured BEFORE the pass, not the
 length of `acc.done` read after it: `list-push` writes into the caller's list
 whenever it has spare capacity (COMPILER-42), so `acc2.done` and `acc.done`
 can be the same object and comparing their lengths compares a list with
 itself. That test is then true on the first pass whatever the pass did.

 WGSL has no forward declarations: a function or module-scope const must be
 declared before it is used, and the IR does not hand us defs in dependency
 order. So helpers are emitted by a topological pass -- a def is emitted once
 every callee it references (that is itself in the emit set) has been emitted.
 Nullary defs become WGSL `const`s. Kernels come last.

  EmitAcc = record {
   text : Text,
   done : List Text
  }

  wgsl-join-names : List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-join-names (xs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length xs then "" else (list-at xs i) & " " & wgsl-join-names xs (i + 1)

  wgsl-all-helper-names : List IRDef, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-all-helper-names (defs) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length defs then acc
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in if (wgsl-is-kernel d | wgsl-is-math-intrinsic (d.name)) then wgsl-all-helper-names defs (i + 1) acc
   else wgsl-all-helper-names defs (i + 1) (list-push acc (d.name))

  wgsl-intersect : List Text, List Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-intersect (xs) (ys) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length xs then acc
   else let x = list-at xs i
   in if wgsl-contains ys x then wgsl-intersect xs ys (i + 1) (list-push acc x)
   else wgsl-intersect xs ys (i + 1) acc

  wgsl-emit-one : WgslCtx, List BufEntry, IRDef -> Text
  wgsl-emit-one (ctx) (bmap) (d) =
   if list-length (d.params) == 0 then
    "const " & wgsl-sanitize (d.name) & " : " & wgsl-ty-text (d.type-val) & " = " & wgsl-expr ctx (d.body) & ";\n"
   else wgsl-emit-helper ctx bmap d

  wgsl-ready-callees : List Text, List Text, List Text, Text, Integer -> Boolean
  wgsl-ready-callees (cs) (emitset) (done) (selfname) (i) =
   if i >= list-length cs then True
   else let c = list-at cs i
   in if ((c == selfname) | (wgsl-contains emitset c == False)) then wgsl-ready-callees cs emitset done selfname (i + 1)
   else if wgsl-contains done c then wgsl-ready-callees cs emitset done selfname (i + 1)
   else False

  wgsl-topo-pass : WgslCtx, List BufEntry, List IRDef, List Text, EmitAcc, Integer -> EmitAcc
  wgsl-topo-pass (ctx) (bmap) (defs) (emitset) (acc) (i) =
   if i >= list-length defs then acc
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in let skip = ((wgsl-is-kernel d) | (wgsl-contains emitset (d.name) == False)) | (wgsl-contains (acc.done) (d.name))
   in if skip then wgsl-topo-pass ctx bmap defs emitset acc (i + 1)
   else let cs = wgsl-collect-calls (d.body) []
   in if wgsl-ready-callees cs emitset (acc.done) (d.name) 0 then
     wgsl-topo-pass ctx bmap defs emitset (EmitAcc { text = (acc.text) & wgsl-emit-one ctx bmap d, done = list-push (acc.done) (d.name) }) (i + 1)
   else wgsl-topo-pass ctx bmap defs emitset acc (i + 1)

  wgsl-topo-loop : WgslCtx, List BufEntry, List IRDef, List Text, EmitAcc, Integer -> EmitAcc
  wgsl-topo-loop (ctx) (bmap) (defs) (emitset) (acc) (iters) =
   if iters <= 0 then acc
   else let before = list-length (acc.done)
   in let acc2 = wgsl-topo-pass ctx bmap defs emitset acc 0
   in if list-length (acc2.done) == before then acc2
   else wgsl-topo-loop ctx bmap defs emitset acc2 (iters - 1)

  wgsl-emit-kernels : WgslCtx, List BufEntry, List IRDef, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-emit-kernels (ctx) (bmap) (defs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length defs then ""
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in if wgsl-is-kernel d then wgsl-emit-kernel ctx bmap d & wgsl-emit-kernels ctx bmap defs (i + 1)
   else wgsl-emit-kernels ctx bmap defs (i + 1)

Section: Undelivered Definitions

 A definition that is reachable, called, and never emitted produces a module
 that calls a function nobody defined, and the plug used to say NOTHING: the
 validator caught it as `unresolved call target`, four faults deep, with no
 hint of which pass dropped it. An instrument that cannot express a failure
 reports success (L-STATES, TheKeyboardWasNeverSilent).

 So this does not answer "something was dropped". It answers with a NAMED
 STATE per definition, because "not blocked" and "blocked by X" send you to
 different places:

   BLOCKED BY <names>  the topological pass never saw these callees finish,
                       so the fault is in readiness or in emission ORDER
   READY, NEVER EMITTED  nothing was blocking it, so the pass stopped early:
                       the iteration cap, or the loop's own exit condition

 It reads only emitset, done and the definition list, so it cannot be fooled
 by the emission path it reports on.

  wgsl-missing-names : List Text, List Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-missing-names (emitset) (done) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length emitset then acc
   else let n = list-at emitset i
   in let acc1 = if wgsl-contains done n then acc else list-push acc n
   in wgsl-missing-names emitset done (i + 1) acc1

  wgsl-calls-of : List IRDef, Text, Integer -> List Text
  wgsl-calls-of (defs) (n) (i) =
   if i >= list-length defs then []
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in if d.name == n then wgsl-collect-calls (d.body) []
   else wgsl-calls-of defs n (i + 1)

  wgsl-blockers-of : List Text, List Text, List Text, Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  wgsl-blockers-of (calls) (emitset) (done) (selfn) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length calls then acc
   else let c = list-at calls i
   in let skip = ((c == selfn) | (wgsl-contains emitset c == False)) | (wgsl-contains done c)
   in let acc1 = if skip then acc else (if wgsl-contains acc c then acc else list-push acc c)
   in wgsl-blockers-of calls emitset done selfn (i + 1) acc1

  wgsl-diag-line : List IRDef, List Text, List Text, Text -> Text
  wgsl-diag-line (defs) (emitset) (done) (n) =
   let cs = wgsl-calls-of defs n 0
   in let bs = wgsl-blockers-of cs emitset done n 0 []
   in if list-length cs == 0 then
    "//   " & wgsl-sanitize n & " -- NO CALLS FOUND: either this definition is not in the chapter list or its body collected nothing. This state is the INSTRUMENT failing to look, not a finding about the pass.\n"
   else if list-length bs == 0 then
    "//   " & wgsl-sanitize n & " -- READY, NEVER EMITTED (" & integer-to-text (list-length cs) & " callee name(s) examined, none outstanding, so the pass stopped early)\n"
   else "//   " & wgsl-sanitize n & " -- BLOCKED BY: " & wgsl-join-names bs 0 & "\n"

  wgsl-diag-lines : List IRDef, List Text, List Text, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-diag-lines (defs) (emitset) (done) (missing) (i) =
   if i >= list-length missing then ""
   else wgsl-diag-line defs emitset done (list-at missing i)
    & wgsl-diag-lines defs emitset done missing (i + 1)

 In wgsl-topo-pass, "ready" and "emitted" are the SAME event: a definition
 judged ready is emitted on the spot. So a definition that was never emitted
 was never judged ready in any pass, and the question is only whether it WOULD
 be judged ready now. `extra` answers that by running one more pass after the
 loop and counting what it adds, which separates the two remaining causes:

   extra > 0   the loop stopped while work was still available, so the fault
               is its exit condition or its iteration budget
   extra == 0  a pass still will not take it, so wgsl-ready-callees disagrees
               with the blocker list computed here, and the two must be
               compared directly

  wgsl-diagnostics : List IRDef, List Text, List Text, Integer -> Text
  wgsl-diagnostics (defs) (emitset) (done) (extra) =
   let missing = wgsl-missing-names emitset done 0 []
   in if list-length missing == 0 then ""
   else "// WGSL PLUG REFUSAL: " & integer-to-text (list-length missing)
    & " reachable definition(s) were NOT emitted, and this module calls them.\n"
    & "// emitset " & integer-to-text (list-length emitset)
    & ", emitted " & integer-to-text (list-length done)
    & ", and ONE MORE PASS after the loop would emit " & integer-to-text extra & " of them.\n"
    & wgsl-diag-lines defs emitset done missing 0
    & "// This is the plug's fault, not the shader's. The module below is invalid.\n\n"
  emit-wgsl-chapter : IRChapter, List ATypeDef -> Text
  emit-wgsl-chapter (ch) (tds) =
   let ctx = empty-wgsl-ctx tds
   in let has-k = wgsl-has-kernel (ch.defs) 0
   in let alldefs = wgsl-all-helper-names (ch.defs) 0 []
   in let emitset = if has-k then wgsl-intersect (wgsl-reachable (ch.defs)) alldefs 0 [] else alldefs
   in let bmap = wgsl-bufmap (ch.defs)
   in let acc0 = EmitAcc { text = "", done = [] }
   in let emitted = wgsl-topo-loop ctx bmap (ch.defs) emitset acc0 (list-length (ch.defs) + 1)
   in let emitted-count = list-length (emitted.done)
   in let extra = wgsl-topo-pass ctx bmap (ch.defs) emitset emitted 0
   in let grew = list-length (extra.done) - emitted-count
   in let helpers = emitted.text
   in "// Generated by Codex WGSL Plug\n"
    & "// Compute shaders lowered from Codex [Device] kernels.\n\n"
    & wgsl-diagnostics (ch.defs) emitset (emitted.done) grew
    & helpers
    & wgsl-emit-kernels ctx bmap (ch.defs) 0
